content.text:
Good.

Create android files. Use Groovy DSL. Root build.gradle:

```
plugins {
    id 'com.android.application' version '9.4.1' apply false
}
```
settings.gradle:
```
pluginManagement { repositories { google(); mavenCentral(); gradlePluginPortal() } }
dependencyResolutionManagement { repositoriesMode.set(RepositoriesMode.FAIL_ON_PROJECT_REPOS); repositories { google(); mavenCentral() } }
rootProject.name='Life Estate'
include ':app'
```
AGP 9.x requires built-in Kotlin? We're Java only, fine. AGP 9 may have new DSL changes: `android { namespace ... compileSdk 36 defaultConfig {...} }`. AGP 9.0 removed `buildFeatures.buildConfig` default? Not an issue. It may require Gradle 9.1. We have 9.8.2. Java 17.

Potential AGP 9.0 change: `android.enableR8.fullMode` etc. Fine.

app/build.gradle:
```
plugins { id 'com.android.application' }
android {
 namespace 'com.lifeestate.game'
 compileSdk 36
 defaultConfig { applicationId ... minSdk 26 targetSdk 36 versionCode 1 versionName '1.0.0' }
 signingConfigs { release { ... } }
 buildTypes { release { minifyEnabled false; shrinkResources false; signingConfig ... } debug {...} }
 compileOptions { sourceCompatibility JavaVersion.VERSION_17; targetCompatibility... }
 packaging { resources { excludes += [...] } }
}
dependencies {
 implementation 'androidx.webkit:webkit:1.14.0'? summary 1.18.0.
 implementation 'androidx.core:core:1.17.0'? 
 implementation 'androidx.core:core-splashscreen:1.0.1'
}
```
Need versions that exist as of Oct 2026. Summary says webkit 1.18.0. androidx.core 1.17.0 maybe. core-splashscreen 1.2.0 maybe. To minimize risk, use known stable core:1.13.1 and splashscreen:1.0.1, webkit:1.12.1. These definitely exist. But compileSdk 36 may warn? fine. Summary recommends 1.18.0; no need latest. Use webkit 1.12.1 known stable. However WebViewAssetLoader API stable. Using older androidx core 1.13.1 with compile 36 fine.

Actually targetSdk 36 (Android 16) may require `androidx.activity` etc for edge-to-edge. We handle manually. minSdk 26.

Signing config: read keystore.properties if exists:
```
def keystorePropsFile = rootProject.file('keystore.properties')
def keystoreProps = new Properties()
if (keystorePropsFile.exists()) keystoreProps.load(...)
android.signingConfigs { release { if (keystorePropsFile.exists()) {...} } }
buildTypes.release { if (keystorePropsFile.exists()) signingConfig signingConfigs.release }
```
Note `rootProject.file` = android/keystore.properties (ignored). Store path could be `storeFile rootProject.file(keystoreProps['storeFile'])`.
If absent, release unsigned; Gradle may name `app-release-unsigned.aab`. Fine.

Assets sync task:
```
def webDir = file('src/main/assets/www')
def distDir = rootProject.file('../dist')
tasks.register('syncWebAssets', Copy) {
    from distDir
    into webDir
    doFirst { delete webDir }
}
tasks.named('preBuild').configure { dependsOn 'syncWebAssets' }
```
AGP 9 may not allow tasks.named('preBuild') because created later. Use `tasks.matching { it.name == 'preBuild' }.configureEach { dependsOn ... }` or `afterEvaluate`. Better use `tasks.register('syncWebAssets', Sync) { from distDir; into webDir }` and `androidComponents.onVariants { variant -> ... }` no. Use `preBuild.dependsOn syncWebAssets` after android block; preBuild task exists by then? AGP creates tasks when plugin applied. `preBuild` is available. Or `tasks.named('preBuild').configure`. Standard.

But if dist missing, `from` nonexistent → Copy does nothing and www empty, app shows blank. Add doFirst check and fail with helpful message. Since npm script builds first. Gradle build directly should fail if dist missing. Use:
```
doFirst { if (!distDir.exists()) throw new GradleException("Run npm run build first...") }
```
Then delete webDir and copy. `Sync` with `into`.

Also need preserve `.gitkeep`? assets/www is generated, add to .gitignore. But APK build needs it. Add `android/app/src/main/assets/www/` to .gitignore.

MainActivity.java:
- package com.lifeestate.game
- imports android.annotation.SuppressLint, app.Activity, content.pm.ActivityInfo? no, Bundle, KeyEvent, net.Uri, os.Build, view.View, view.WindowInsets, webkit.*, androidx.webkit.*, androidx.core.view.*, androidx.core.splashscreen.SplashScreen.
- `onCreate`: installSplashScreen() before super. `super.onCreate`. WindowCompat.setDecorFitsSystemWindows(getWindow(), false); set background color; keep screen on; hideSystemBars; create WebView programmatically or use layout XML. Use layout XML for clarity with WebView id. `setContentView(R.layout.activity_main)`.
- `configureWebView`: settings JS, domStorage, database? no. `setSupportZoom(false)`, `setBuiltInZoomControls(false)`, `setDisplayZoomControls(false)`, `setMediaPlaybackRequiresUserGesture(true)`, `setAllowFileAccess(false)`, `setAllowContentAccess(false)`, `setMixedContentMode(MIXED_CONTENT_NEVER_ALLOW)`, `setCacheMode(LOAD_DEFAULT)`, `setTextZoom(100)` (respect? maybe).
- `WebView.setWebContentsDebuggingEnabled(BuildConfig.DEBUG)`.
- `webView.setBackgroundColor(Color.rgb(7,27,28))`.
- `WebViewAssetLoader assetLoader = new WebViewAssetLoader.Builder().addPathHandler("/assets/", new AssetsPathHandler(this)).build();`
- `webView.setWebViewClient(new WebViewClient() { shouldInterceptRequest -> assetLoader.shouldInterceptRequest(uri); shouldOverrideUrlLoading -> if host appassets... false; else open external? no -> true; })`.
- Load `https://appassets.androidplatform.net/assets/www/index.html`.
- `webView.setWebChromeClient(new WebChromeClient())` maybe for console and fullscreen video (not needed). Add for JS dialogs? not used. Fine.
- Back: OnBackPressedDispatcher requires ComponentActivity. We can use `OnBackInvokedDispatcher` for API 33+ or override onBackPressed deprecated. Simpler override `onBackPressed()` still works with target 36? It's deprecated but functional if not using predictive back. Add `android:enableOnBackInvokedCallback="false"` in manifest to force legacy. Or use OnBackInvokedDispatcher for 33+, and override for older. Better implement modern:
  - In onCreate: if Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= 33, `getOnBackInvokedDispatcher().registerOnBackInvokedCallback(PRIORITY_DEFAULT, this::handleBack)`.
  - Else override onBackPressed -> handleBack.
  - Manifest `android:enableOnBackInvokedCallback="true"` default. For 33+ use callback.
  - handleBack evaluates JS. While callback async, we can't synchronously decide; always evaluate and finish if false. Since callback gets invoked and JS returns; fine.
  - Need prevent finish before evaluate. In callback, call `evaluateJavascript` and in callback if false `finish()`. For API <33 override onBackPressed same.
